  "comment": "HEXAGONAL BUBBLE TILES (Chase, Field & McCluer, 'Puzzle Pieces and Bubble Tiles', working draft 2026-08-22) \u2014 Hokusai's original family, 1824. Sibling of bubble-tri and bubble-sq: same complementary matching rule (a bump must meet a bite), hexagonal substrate. The fourteen tiles are the binary necklaces of length 6 (OEIS A000031), generated here rather than written out. Necklaces up to ROTATION only, so the chiral pair at three bites stays two tiles \u2014 the paper's H3A and H3A*, which it treats as distinct because the engine cannot place a tile reflected. NAMING DIVERGES from the paper at three bites: this writes 3A/3B/3C/3D where the paper writes 3A/3A*/3B/3C. Same partition, different labels. Angles in D=24 units: 120 = 8, three to a vertex, so maxValence 3 is exact. The SEARCH needs EU_EDGE_COMPL=1 and the developer --complement.",
